---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title={"About · Paramore.Design"}
  description={"About Hunter Paramore, Product designer with 13 years of experience building apps, design systems, and digital products across startups and consumer products at scale."}
>
<!-- About Intro -->
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: calc(var(--space-4xl) + 80px);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-intro">
        <div class="about-intro__text">
          <span class="label mb-md" style="display: block;">About</span>
          <h1 class="display-lg">Hunter Paramore</h1>
          <p class="mt-lg">
            I&rsquo;m a product designer with 13 years of experience, and for ten of
            them I was the only designer at Mutual. I was the first designer there,
            starting from essentially nothing. The last five I was full-time, and
            that&rsquo;s the stretch where it went from a small app to the
            <strong>#1 LDS dating app</strong>, responsible for 40,000+ marriages.
          </p>
          <p>
            Partway through we decided the same product could serve more people, so
            we built a second dating app for Christians called <strong>Ark</strong>,
            now one of the top Christian dating apps in the App Store. I ran both
            brands and both design systems off parallel clones of one codebase.
          </p>
          <p>
            Design systems are the part of the work I keep returning to. I built
            Mutual&rsquo;s across three brands and six themes, with semantic tokens
            and live WCAG contrast checking built in, so accessibility problems show
            up while you&rsquo;re designing instead of in an audit months later. One
            of my systems was featured on Figma&rsquo;s community homepage and has
            since passed <strong>300,000 views and 17,000 downloads</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            For the past year and a half I&rsquo;ve gone deep on AI. I use it to
            build the things I design &mdash; apps, websites, internal tools, the
            kind of work that used to need a team and months of runway &mdash; and
            I&rsquo;ve been building design systems structured so AI agents can
            consume them directly and produce on-brand, accessible UI from one
            source. AI makes the work fast. Thirteen years of design is what keeps
            it usable.
          </p>
          <p>
            I studied art with an emphasis on design, and I&rsquo;ve spent my career
            in the space where design meets product meets engineering. I&rsquo;m
            currently looking for Senior or Staff product design work, full-time or
            fractional, and early-stage startups are very much on the table.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-intro__photo">
          <!-- Replace with: <img src="/assets/images/headshot.jpg" alt="Hunter Paramore"> -->
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding: 0 var(--content-padding);">

  <!-- Skills -->
  <section class="section--sm" aria-labelledby="skills-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="skills-heading" class="mb-2xl">What I Bring</h2>
      <div class="skills-grid">
        <div class="skill-group">
          <h3 class="skill-group__title">Design</h3>
          <ul class="skill-group__list" role="list">
            <li>Product & UX Strategy</li>
            <li>UI Design & Interaction</li>
            <li>Design Systems</li>
            <li>User Research & Testing</li>
            <li>Prototyping</li>
            <li>Brand & Visual Identity</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group">
          <h3 class="skill-group__title">Build</h3>
          <ul class="skill-group__list" role="list">
            <li>iOS · Swift / SwiftUI</li>
            <li>Android · Kotlin / Compose</li>
            <li>Web · React / HTML / CSS</li>
            <li>Backend · Firebase / Cloud Functions</li>
            <li>Games · Unity / SpriteKit</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-group">
          <h3 class="skill-group__title">Think</h3>
          <ul class="skill-group__list" role="list">
            <li>Product Roadmapping</li>
            <li>User Journey Mapping</li>
            <li>Data-Informed Decisions</li>
            <li>Cross-Platform Strategy</li>
            <li>Team Collaboration</li>
            <li>Stakeholder Communication</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; padding: 0 var(--content-padding);">

  <!-- Contact -->
  <section class="contact-section" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="contact-heading" class="display-md">Let's Build Something</h2>
      <p>
        Whether you need a designer on your team, a partner to bring your
        vision to life, or just want to talk product, I'd like to hear from you.
      </p>
      <div class="contact-links">
        <a href="mailto:hello@paramore.design" class="btn btn--primary">
          Email Me <span class="btn__arrow">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--secondary">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="https://dribbble.com/HunterParamore" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--secondary">Dribbble</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Footer -->
</Base>
